  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday through next Thursday)\nIssued at 1137 PM CDT THU JUN 4 2026\n\nUpper-level ridging will continue to dominate the forecast for\nthe next 24-hours, before slowly starting to retrograde to the SE\ninto Saturday morning. At the same time, a closed low pressure\nwill begin to trek east across Texas, with the outer fringes of\nthe trough reaching our area by Saturday afternoon. This closed\nlow will allow for a series of shortwave disturbances to work\nthrough the region through the weekend, increasing rain chances\ninto the start of next week.\n\nUpper-level ridging will start to build back in over the area by\nTuesday, shutting down the more organized rain activity. However,\nthat does not mean rain chances will completely end, as diurnally\ndriven afternoon convection remains in the forecast into next\nweekend. Temperatures will slowly begin to climb during this time\nperiod as well, with afternoon highs reaching the upper-80s by\nThursday.\n\n/44/",
